?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2FHero%2FExplore%2Fnz-mtb-rally-2026%2FNZ-MTB-RALLY-2026-DAY-6-Nelson-Koata-Park-Mikhail-Huggins__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuMTUiLDEwMDAsNjAwXQ.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=85"/></div></div><div class="pb-4 pt-2 font-sans text-sm text-neutral">Go round and round, all year round, in Nelson City.</div></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 grow-0 pl-4 relative shrink-0 basis-1/2 sm:basis-1/3 md:pl-0 md:mt-0"><div class="group relative w-full shrink-0 grow-0 overflow-hidden h-56 md:h-64 md:w-full lg:h-96 xl:h-[420px]"><div class="relative flex h-full w-full items-center justify-center overflow-hidden rounded" style="width:100%;height:100%"><img alt="blurry placeholder" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="absolute inset-0 z-0 h-full w-full bg-light object-cover rounded transition-all duration-500 ease-in-out" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="data:image/png;base64,"/><img alt="Dine by the water&#x27;s edge at the Boat Shed in Nelson." loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="object-cover rounded transition-all duration-500 ease-in-out z-[-10]" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;object-position:center;color:transparent" sizes="100%" srcSet="/_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2Flistings%2Fboat-shed-cafe%2FBoat-Shed-Cafe-Nelson__FocusFillMaxWyIwLjAwIiwiMC4wMCIsNjAwLDgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=16&amp;q=85 16w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2Flistings%2Fboat-shed-cafe%2FBoat-Shed-Cafe-Nelson__FocusFillMaxWyIwLjAwIiwiMC4wMCIsNjAwLDgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=32&amp;q=85 32w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2Flistings%2Fboat-shed-cafe%2FBoat-Shed-Cafe-Nelson__FocusFillMaxWyIwLjAwIiwiMC4wMCIsNjAwLDgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=48&amp;q=85 48w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2Flistings%2Fboat-shed-cafe%2FBoat-Shed-Cafe-Nelson__FocusFillMaxWyIwLjAwIiwiMC4wMCIsNjAwLDgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=64&amp;q=85 64w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2Flistings%2Fboat-shed-cafe%2FBoat-Shed-Cafe-Nelson__FocusFillMaxWyIwLjAwIiwiMC4wMCIsNjAwLDgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=96&amp;q=85 96w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2Flistings%2Fboat-shed-cafe%2FBoat-Shed-Cafe-Nelson__FocusFillMaxWyIwLjAwIiwiMC4wMCIsNjAwLDgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=128&amp;q=85 128w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2Flistings%2Fboat-shed-cafe%2FBoat-Shed-Cafe-Nelson__FocusFillMaxWyIwLjAwIiwiMC4wMCIsNjAwLDgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=256&amp;q=85 256w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2Flistings%2Fboat-shed-cafe%2FBoat-Shed-Cafe-Nelson__FocusFillMaxWyIwLjAwIiwiMC4wMCIsNjAwLDgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=384&amp;q=85 384w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2Flistings%2Fboat-shed-cafe%2FBoat-Shed-Cafe-Nelson__FocusFillMaxWyIwLjAwIiwiMC4wMCIsNjAwLDgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=640&amp;q=85 640w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2Flistings%2Fboat-shed-cafe%2FBoat-Shed-Cafe-Nelson__FocusFillMaxWyIwLjAwIiwiMC4wMCIsNjAwLDgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=750&amp;q=85 750w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2Flistings%2Fboat-shed-cafe%2FBoat-Shed-Cafe-Nelson__FocusFillMaxWyIwLjAwIiwiMC4wMCIsNjAwLDgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=828&amp;q=85 828w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2Flistings%2Fboat-shed-cafe%2FBoat-Shed-Cafe-Nelson__FocusFillMaxWyIwLjAwIiwiMC4wMCIsNjAwLDgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=1080&amp;q=85 1080w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2Flistings%2Fboat-shed-cafe%2FBoat-Shed-Cafe-Nelson__FocusFillMaxWyIwLjAwIiwiMC4wMCIsNjAwLDgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=1200&amp;q=85 1200w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2Flistings%2Fboat-shed-cafe%2FBoat-Shed-Cafe-Nelson__FocusFillMaxWyIwLjAwIiwiMC4wMCIsNjAwLDgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=1920&amp;q=85 1920w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2Flistings%2Fboat-shed-cafe%2FBoat-Shed-Cafe-Nelson__FocusFillMaxWyIwLjAwIiwiMC4wMCIsNjAwLDgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=2048&amp;q=85 2048w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2Flistings%2Fboat-shed-cafe%2FBoat-Shed-Cafe-Nelson__FocusFillMaxWyIwLjAwIiwiMC4wMCIsNjAwLDgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=85 3840w" src="/_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2Flistings%2Fboat-shed-cafe%2FBoat-Shed-Cafe-Nelson__FocusFillMaxWyIwLjAwIiwiMC4wMCIsNjAwLDgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=85"/></div></div><div class="pb-4 pt-2 font-sans text-sm text-neutral">Dine by the water&#x27;s edge at the Boat Shed in Nelson.</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="ElementContent"><div class="relative"><div class="relative"><div class="container pt-6 md:pt-12 lg:pt-16 pb-6 md:pb-12 lg:pb-20"><div class="flex flex-wrap text-start justify-between max-w-none prose lg:prose-lg xl:prose-xl"><h3 class="w-full !text-xl lg:!leading-9 xl:w-1/4 shrink-0">Nelson city puts some of New Zealand’s best outdoor adventures within easy reach</h3><div class="w-full max-w-none justify-end text-start empty:hidden xl:w-2/3 [&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:!mt-0"><p>Few city views rival the sweep across Nelson and Tasman Bay from the top of the <a href="/scenic-attractions/centre-of-new-zealand">Centre of New Zealand</a>, or snow-dusted hills rising behind <a href="/scenic-attractions/tahunanui-beach">Tāhunanui Beach</a> on a crisp winter morning. Here, getting outdoors doesn’t require leaving the city far behind — walking trails, beaches, rivers and hills are all remarkably close.</p>
<p>Mountain bikers have some of New Zealand’s best riding on the doorstep, from the classic <a href="/explore/things-to-do/cycling-and-mountain-biking/great-rides/coppermine-trail-great-ride">Coppermine Trail</a> to the purpose-built trails of <a href="/activities-day-trips/koata-mtb-park">Koata Park</a> and <a href="/activities-day-trips/cable-bay-mtb-park">Cable Bay Adventure Park</a>. With riding year round and trails for different abilities and appetites for adventure, it’s easy to spend the morning on two wheels and be back in town for a riverside coffee, local beer or long lunch.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="ElementalOperatorListings"><div class="relative"><div class="relative"><!--$?--><template id="B:1"></template><div class="spinner-container flex grow flex-wrap items-center justify-center"><div><h2 class="flex w-full grow items-center justify-center py-5">Please wait...</h2><span class="loading loading-ball loading-xs"></span><span class="loading loading-ball loading-sm"></span><span class="loading loading-ball loading-md"></span><span class="loading loading-ball loading-lg"></span></div></div><!--/$--></div></div></div><div class="ElementAccordion"><div class="relative"><div class="relative"><div class="container pb-12 pt-6 md:pt-12 lg:pb-20"><div class="flex flex-wrap text-start justify-between max-w-none prose lg:prose-lg xl:prose-xl mb-5"><h3 class="w-full !text-xl lg:!leading-9 xl:w-1/4 shrink-0">Frequently asked questions about Nelson New Zealand</h3><div class="w-full max-w-none justify-end text-start empty:hidden xl:w-2/3 [&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:!mt-0"><p>Planning a visit to Nelson City? From getting here and getting around to things to do, rainy-day ideas and the story behind Whakatū, here are a few handy answers to help you make the most of your time in the city.</p></div></div><div class="w-full justify-end text-start xl:ms-auto xl:w-2/3" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" class="border-b"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" class="flex"><button type="button" aria-controls="radix-_R_4d8iqnpftb_" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" id="radix-_R_d8iqnpftb_" class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-between py-4 text-start transition-all hover:underline [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;svg]:rotate-180 font-semibold xl:text-lg" data-radix-collection-item="">Where is Nelson City and how do I get there?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-state="closed" id="radix-_R_4d8iqnpftb_" role="region" aria-labelledby="radix-_R_d8iqnpftb_" data-orientation="vertical" class="text-sm [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:invisible [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[0fr] [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[1fr]" style="--radix-accordion-content-height:var(--radix-collapsible-content-height);--radix-accordion-content-width:var(--radix-collapsible-content-width)"><div class="grid transition-[grid-template-rows,visibility] duration-200 ease-out"><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="pb-4 pt-0 prose xl:prose-lg"><p>Nelson sits at the top of New Zealand’s South Island, looking out across Tasman Bay. Nelson Airport is around 15 minutes from the city centre, with regular domestic flights connecting to major New Zealand cities like Auckland, Wellington and Christchurch. Driving is another great option, especially if Nelson is part of a wider South Island road trip.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" class="border-b"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" class="flex"><button type="button" aria-controls="radix-_R_4l8iqnpftb_" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" id="radix-_R_l8iqnpftb_" class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-between py-4 text-start transition-all hover:underline [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;svg]:rotate-180 font-semibold xl:text-lg" data-radix-collection-item="">What does Whakatū mean?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-state="closed" id="radix-_R_4l8iqnpftb_" role="region" aria-labelledby="radix-_R_l8iqnpftb_" data-orientation="vertical" class="text-sm [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:invisible [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[0fr] [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[1fr]" style="--radix-accordion-content-height:var(--radix-collapsible-content-height);--radix-accordion-content-width:var(--radix-collapsible-content-width)"><div class="grid transition-[grid-template-rows,visibility] duration-200 ease-out"><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="pb-4 pt-0 prose xl:prose-lg"><p>Whakatū is the Māori name for Nelson. The name is commonly interpreted as meaning ‘to build’, ‘to establish’ or ‘to set up’. Using Whakatū acknowledges the deep Māori history and identity of this place, which stretches back long before the establishment of the European settlement of Nelson.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" class="border-b"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" class="flex"><button type="button" aria-controls="radix-_R_4t8iqnpftb_" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" id="radix-_R_t8iqnpftb_" class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-between py-4 text-start transition-all hover:underline [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;svg]:rotate-180 font-semibold xl:text-lg" data-radix-collection-item="">What is Nelson City known for?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-state="closed" id="radix-_R_4t8iqnpftb_" role="region" aria-labelledby="radix-_R_t8iqnpftb_" data-orientation="vertical" class="text-sm [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:invisible [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[0fr] [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[1fr]" style="--radix-accordion-content-height:var(--radix-collapsible-content-height);--radix-accordion-content-width:var(--radix-collapsible-content-width)"><div class="grid transition-[grid-template-rows,visibility] duration-200 ease-out"><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="pb-4 pt-0 prose xl:prose-lg"><p>Nelson is known for sunshine, creativity, great food and incredible access to the outdoors. With <a href="/explore/places-to-go/national-parks">three national parks</a> surrounding the region and <a href="/explore/things-to-do/cycling-and-mountain-biking/mountain-biking">world-class mountain biking</a> right on the city’s doorstep, adventure is never far away. Add <a href="/explore/things-to-do/arts-artisans">galleries and studios</a>, independent shops, excellent local produce, <a href="/explore/eat-and-drink/wineries">wine</a> and <a href="/explore/eat-and-drink/breweries">craft beer</a>, and you’ve got a small city with plenty packed into it.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" class="border-b"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" class="flex"><button type="button" aria-controls="radix-_R_558iqnpftb_" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" id="radix-_R_158iqnpftb_" class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-between py-4 text-start transition-all hover:underline [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;svg]:rotate-180 font-semibold xl:text-lg" data-radix-collection-item="">What are the best things to do in Nelson City?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-state="closed" id="radix-_R_558iqnpftb_" role="region" aria-labelledby="radix-_R_158iqnpftb_" data-orientation="vertical" class="text-sm [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:invisible [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[0fr] [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[1fr]" style="--radix-accordion-content-height:var(--radix-collapsible-content-height);--radix-accordion-content-width:var(--radix-collapsible-content-width)"><div class="grid transition-[grid-template-rows,visibility] duration-200 ease-out"><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="pb-4 pt-0 prose xl:prose-lg"><p>Start in the compact city centre, where you can browse galleries, independent shops and cafés before exploring the riverside and heritage streets. Visit the Nelson Market on a Saturday, discover local art at The Suter, wander through Queens Gardens, or hit one of the walking and cycling trails close to town. Explore our <a href="/explore/places-to-go/cities-towns/nelson-city/things-to-do-nelson-city">Things to do in Nelson City story</a> for more inspiration.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" class="border-b"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" class="flex"><button type="button" aria-controls="radix-_R_5d8iqnpftb_" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" id="radix-_R_1d8iqnpftb_" class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-between py-4 text-start transition-all hover:underline [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;svg]:rotate-180 font-semibold xl:text-lg" data-radix-collection-item="">Is Nelson worth visiting and how many days should I spend?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-state="closed" id="radix-_R_5d8iqnpftb_" role="region" aria-labelledby="radix-_R_1d8iqnpftb_" data-orientation="vertical" class="text-sm [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:invisible [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[0fr] [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[1fr]" style="--radix-accordion-content-height:var(--radix-collapsible-content-height);--radix-accordion-content-width:var(--radix-collapsible-content-width)"><div class="grid transition-[grid-template-rows,visibility] duration-200 ease-out"><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="pb-4 pt-0 prose xl:prose-lg"><p>Absolutely! Nelson Tasman was <a href="https://www.nelsontasman.nz/about-us/news-from-nt/nelson-tasman-tops-new-zealands-domestic-visitor-satisfaction-rankings/">voted #1 for traveler satisfaction in 2025</a> and it&#x27;s easy to see why. We recommend spending at least three to four days in Nelson to explore the city at a relaxed pace. Stay longer and use Nelson as your base to discover the wider region, from golden beaches and boutique wineries to creative communities and three spectacular national parks. There&#x27;s plenty to keep you here.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" class="border-b"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" class="flex"><button type="button" aria-controls="radix-_R_5l8iqnpftb_" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" id="radix-_R_1l8iqnpftb_" class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-between py-4 text-start transition-all hover:underline [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;svg]:rotate-180 font-semibold xl:text-lg" data-radix-collection-item="">What is the best time of year to visit Nelson?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-state="closed" id="radix-_R_5l8iqnpftb_" role="region" aria-labelledby="radix-_R_1l8iqnpftb_" data-orientation="vertical" class="text-sm [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:invisible [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[0fr] [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[1fr]" style="--radix-accordion-content-height:var(--radix-collapsible-content-height);--radix-accordion-content-width:var(--radix-collapsible-content-width)"><div class="grid transition-[grid-template-rows,visibility] duration-200 ease-out"><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="pb-4 pt-0 prose xl:prose-lg"><p>Nelson is a year-round destination, with each season bringing something different. Summer is made for beaches, outdoor dining and long days outside, while autumn brings settled days and beautiful colour. Winter is quieter and well suited to galleries, food and nearby walks, while spring brings longer days and great conditions for getting back out on the hiking trails.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" class="border-b"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" class="flex"><button type="button" aria-controls="radix-_R_5t8iqnpftb_" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" id="radix-_R_1t8iqnpftb_" class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-between py-4 text-start transition-all hover:underline [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;svg]:rotate-180 font-semibold xl:text-lg" data-radix-collection-item="">Can I explore Nelson City without a car?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-state="closed" id="radix-_R_5t8iqnpftb_" role="region" aria-labelledby="radix-_R_1t8iqnpftb_" data-orientation="vertical" class="text-sm [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:invisible [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[0fr] [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[1fr]" style="--radix-accordion-content-height:var(--radix-collapsible-content-height);--radix-accordion-content-width:var(--radix-collapsible-content-width)"><div class="grid transition-[grid-template-rows,visibility] duration-200 ease-out"><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="pb-4 pt-0 prose xl:prose-lg"><p>Yes. Central Nelson is compact and easy to explore on foot, with shops, galleries, cafés, parks and the river all close together. Bikes are another good option, and <a href="/explore/plan-your-trip/getting-around">local buses</a> can take you further afield. Heading to Abel Tasman National Park? Many tour operators offer transport from Nelson, and during summer and autumn, the <a href="/transport/the-better-bus">Better Bus</a> connects Nelson with Kaiteriteri, Mārahau and Motueka. A car is handy for exploring further afield, but you can see plenty of Nelson Tasman without one.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" class="border-b"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" class="flex"><button type="button" aria-controls="radix-_R_658iqnpftb_" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" id="radix-_R_258iqnpftb_" class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-between py-4 text-start transition-all hover:underline [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;svg]:rotate-180 font-semibold xl:text-lg" data-radix-collection-item="">Where are the best places to eat and drink in Nelson?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-state="closed" id="radix-_R_658iqnpftb_" role="region" aria-labelledby="radix-_R_258iqnpftb_" data-orientation="vertical" class="text-sm [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:invisible [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[0fr] [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[1fr]" style="--radix-accordion-content-height:var(--radix-collapsible-content-height);--radix-accordion-content-width:var(--radix-collapsible-content-width)"><div class="grid transition-[grid-template-rows,visibility] duration-200 ease-out"><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="pb-4 pt-0 prose xl:prose-lg"><p>You’re spoilt for choice. Nelson has everything from <a href="/explore/eat-and-drink/cafes">relaxed cafés</a> and <a href="/explore/eat-and-drink/restaurants-and-bars">neighbourhood eateries to restaurants</a> celebrating local seafood and seasonal produce. The wider region is also well known for its <a href="/explore/eat-and-drink/breweries">craft breweries</a>, <a href="/explore/eat-and-drink/wineries">wineries</a> and <a href="/explore/eat-and-drink/artisan-markets">artisan producers</a>, so arriving hungry is a solid strategy.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" class="border-b"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" class="flex"><button type="button" aria-controls="radix-_R_6d8iqnpftb_" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" id="radix-_R_2d8iqnpftb_" class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-between py-4 text-start transition-all hover:underline [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;svg]:rotate-180 font-semibold xl:text-lg" data-radix-collection-item="">What can I do in Nelson on a rainy day?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-state="closed" id="radix-_R_6d8iqnpftb_" role="region" aria-labelledby="radix-_R_2d8iqnpftb_" data-orientation="vertical" class="text-sm [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:invisible [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[0fr] [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[1fr]" style="--radix-accordion-content-height:var(--radix-collapsible-content-height);--radix-accordion-content-width:var(--radix-collapsible-content-width)"><div class="grid transition-[grid-template-rows,visibility] duration-200 ease-out"><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="pb-4 pt-0 prose xl:prose-lg"><p>Rain is a good excuse to explore Nelson’s creative side. Visit The Suter Art Gallery, browse local galleries and studios, discover the city’s shops, settle into a café or sample some locally made beer. And when the clouds clear, you’re never far from a walk or a waterfront wander.</p>
<p>Visiting with the kids? Check out our <a href="/explore/features/rainy-day-fun">Rainy day family fun story</a> for more ideas to keep everyone entertained.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" class="border-b"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" class="flex"><button type="button" aria-controls="radix-_R_6l8iqnpftb_" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" id="radix-_R_2l8iqnpftb_" class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-between py-4 text-start transition-all hover:underline [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;svg]:rotate-180 font-semibold xl:text-lg" data-radix-collection-item="">Is there a visitor information centre in Nelson?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-state="closed" id="radix-_R_6l8iqnpftb_" role="region" aria-labelledby="radix-_R_2l8iqnpftb_" data-orientation="vertical" class="text-sm [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:invisible [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[0fr] [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[1fr]" style="--radix-accordion-content-height:var(--radix-collapsible-content-height);--radix-accordion-content-width:var(--radix-collapsible-content-width)"><div class="grid transition-[grid-template-rows,visibility] duration-200 ease-out"><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="pb-4 pt-0 prose xl:prose-lg"><p>Nelson City doesn’t have a traditional isite anymore, but you can still find plenty of help when you arrive. <a href="/accommodation/yha-nelson-by-accents">YHA Nelson</a> offers visitor information and local advice.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" class="border-b"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" class="flex"><button type="button" aria-controls="radix-_R_6t8iqnpftb_" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" id="radix-_R_2t8iqnpftb_" class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-between py-4 text-start transition-all hover:underline [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;svg]:rotate-180 font-semibold xl:text-lg" data-radix-collection-item="">How many people live in Nelson?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-state="closed" id="radix-_R_6t8iqnpftb_" role="region" aria-labelledby="radix-_R_2t8iqnpftb_" data-orientation="vertical" class="text-sm [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:invisible [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[0fr] [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[1fr]" style="--radix-accordion-content-height:var(--radix-collapsible-content-height);--radix-accordion-content-width:var(--radix-collapsible-content-width)"><div class="grid transition-[grid-template-rows,visibility] duration-200 ease-out"><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="pb-4 pt-0 prose xl:prose-lg"><p>Nelson is home to approximately 52,584 people, <a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.stats.govt.nz/infographics/detailed-regional-infographics-from-2023-census/our-region-nelson" target="_blank">according to Stats NZ&#x27;s 2025 population estimates</a>.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" class="border-b"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" class="flex"><button type="button" aria-controls="radix-_R_758iqnpftb_" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" id="radix-_R_358iqnpftb_" class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-between py-4 text-start transition-all hover:underline [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;svg]:rotate-180 font-semibold xl:text-lg" data-radix-collection-item="">Where is the Centre of New Zealand?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-state="closed" id="radix-_R_758iqnpftb_" role="region" aria-labelledby="radix-_R_358iqnpftb_" data-orientation="vertical" class="text-sm [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:invisible [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[0fr] [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[1fr]" style="--radix-accordion-content-height:var(--radix-collapsible-content-height);--radix-accordion-content-width:var(--radix-collapsible-content-width)"><div class="grid transition-[grid-template-rows,visibility] duration-200 ease-out"><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="pb-4 pt-0 prose xl:prose-lg"><p>The <a href="/scenic-attractions/centre-of-new-zealand">Centre of New Zealand</a> is a popular landmark on Botanical Hill in Nelson, just a short walk from the city centre. A 20–30 minute uphill walk takes you to the summit, where you&#x27;ll enjoy panoramic views over Nelson, Tasman Bay and the surrounding mountains. It&#x27;s a favourite local walk that&#x27;s both family-friendly and dog-friendly, making it a great outing for all ages and four-legged companions. Despite its name, it&#x27;s not the exact geographical centre of the country. The site was used as a central survey point in the 1800s and remains one of Nelson&#x27;s most-loved short walks.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" class="border-b"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" class="flex"><button type="button" aria-controls="radix-_R_7d8iqnpftb_" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" id="radix-_R_3d8iqnpftb_" class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-between py-4 text-start transition-all hover:underline [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;svg]:rotate-180 font-semibold xl:text-lg" data-radix-collection-item="">What are the best restaurants in Nelson City?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-state="closed" id="radix-_R_7d8iqnpftb_" role="region" aria-labelledby="radix-_R_3d8iqnpftb_" data-orientation="vertical" class="text-sm [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:invisible [&amp;[data-state=closed]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[0fr] [&amp;[data-state=open]&gt;div]:grid-rows-[1fr]" style="--radix-accordion-content-height:var(--radix-collapsible-content-height);--radix-accordion-content-width:var(--radix-collapsible-content-width)"><div class="grid transition-[grid-template-rows,visibility] duration-200 ease-out"><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="pb-4 pt-0 prose xl:prose-lg"><p>Nelson City is home to some of the best dining in the region, with talented chefs making the most of fresh local produce, seafood and wines. Local favourites include <a href="/eat-drink/hopgoods-restaurant">Hopgoods</a> and <a href="/eat-drink/eight-plates">Eight Plates</a> for seasonal fine dining, <a href="/eat-drink/arden-bar-and-kitchen">Arden</a> for creative sharing plates, <a href="/eat-drink/hawker-house">Hawker House</a> for bold Asian flavours and <a href="/eat-drink/urban-oyster-bar-and-eatery">Urban Oyster Bar &amp; Eatery</a> for seafood and lively dining. For a meal with a view, head to the <a href="/eat-drink/boat-shed-cafe">Boat Shed Café</a> on Nelson&#x27;s waterfront. From relaxed eateries to award-winning restaurants, there&#x27;s plenty to satisfy every appetite. And if brunch is more your style, check out our<a href="/explore/features/brunch-done-right"> best brunch spots</a> story for more delicious local favourites.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="ElementContent bg-sky text-white"><div class="relative"><div class="relative"><div class="container pt-6 md:pt-12 lg:pt-16 pb-6 md:pb-12 lg:pb-20"><div class="flex flex-wrap text-start justify-between max-w-none prose lg:prose-lg xl:prose-xl prose-invert text-white"><h3 class="w-full !text-xl lg:!leading-9 xl:w-1/4 shrink-0">Quick fact in celebration of Te Wiki o te Reo Māori</h3><div class="w-full max-w-none justify-end text-start empty:hidden xl:w-2/3 [&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:!mt-0"><p>The Maori name for Nelson has two alternative spellings. Wakatū or Whakatū. Neither is wrong, and both spellings have traditions and stories behind them. These stories can be found on <a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.theprow.org.nz/maori/whats-in-a-name-wakatu-or-whakatu/" target="_blank">The Prow.</a> </p>
<p>Pronunciation Guide: (Far-car-two). </p></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="ElementalPageGrid"><div class="relative"><div class="relative"><div class=""><div class="py-6 empty:hidden md:pt-12 container"></div><div class="relative w-full" role="region" aria-roledescription="carousel"><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="flex -ml-4"><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 relative max-h-[1400px] min-h-[500px] w-full 2xl:max-h-[75vh] 2xl:min-h-[800px]"><div class="relative flex h-full w-full items-center justify-center bg-light md:aspect-video" style="width:100%;height:100%"><img alt="blurry placeholder" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="absolute inset-0 z-0 h-full w-full bg-light object-cover" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="data:image/png;base64,"/><img alt="Tasman Great Taste Trail at Kaiteretere by Aimee Jules credit NelsonTasmanNZ (2)" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="object-cover z-[-10]" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;object-position:center;color:transparent" sizes="100%" srcSet="/_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2FUploads%2FTasman-Great-Taste-Trail-at-Kaiteretere-by-Aimee-Jules-credit-NelsonTasmanNZ-2__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuNDkiLDI4ODAsMTgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=16&amp;q=85 16w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2FUploads%2FTasman-Great-Taste-Trail-at-Kaiteretere-by-Aimee-Jules-credit-NelsonTasmanNZ-2__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuNDkiLDI4ODAsMTgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=32&amp;q=85 32w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2FUploads%2FTasman-Great-Taste-Trail-at-Kaiteretere-by-Aimee-Jules-credit-NelsonTasmanNZ-2__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuNDkiLDI4ODAsMTgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=48&amp;q=85 48w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2FUploads%2FTasman-Great-Taste-Trail-at-Kaiteretere-by-Aimee-Jules-credit-NelsonTasmanNZ-2__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuNDkiLDI4ODAsMTgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=64&amp;q=85 64w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2FUploads%2FTasman-Great-Taste-Trail-at-Kaiteretere-by-Aimee-Jules-credit-NelsonTasmanNZ-2__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuNDkiLDI4ODAsMTgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=96&amp;q=85 96w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2FUploads%2FTasman-Great-Taste-Trail-at-Kaiteretere-by-Aimee-Jules-credit-NelsonTasmanNZ-2__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuNDkiLDI4ODAsMTgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=128&amp;q=85 128w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2FUploads%2FTasman-Great-Taste-Trail-at-Kaiteretere-by-Aimee-Jules-credit-NelsonTasmanNZ-2__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuNDkiLDI4ODAsMTgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=256&amp;q=85 256w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2FUploads%2FTasman-Great-Taste-Trail-at-Kaiteretere-by-Aimee-Jules-credit-NelsonTasmanNZ-2__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuNDkiLDI4ODAsMTgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=384&amp;q=85 384w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2FUploads%2FTasman-Great-Taste-Trail-at-Kaiteretere-by-Aimee-Jules-credit-NelsonTasmanNZ-2__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuNDkiLDI4ODAsMTgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=640&amp;q=85 640w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2FUploads%2FTasman-Great-Taste-Trail-at-Kaiteretere-by-Aimee-Jules-credit-NelsonTasmanNZ-2__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuNDkiLDI4ODAsMTgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=750&amp;q=85 750w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2FUploads%2FTasman-Great-Taste-Trail-at-Kaiteretere-by-Aimee-Jules-credit-NelsonTasmanNZ-2__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuNDkiLDI4ODAsMTgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=828&amp;q=85 828w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2FUploads%2FTasman-Great-Taste-Trail-at-Kaiteretere-by-Aimee-Jules-credit-NelsonTasmanNZ-2__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuNDkiLDI4ODAsMTgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=1080&amp;q=85 1080w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2FUploads%2FTasman-Great-Taste-Trail-at-Kaiteretere-by-Aimee-Jules-credit-NelsonTasmanNZ-2__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuNDkiLDI4ODAsMTgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=1200&amp;q=85 1200w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2FUploads%2FTasman-Great-Taste-Trail-at-Kaiteretere-by-Aimee-Jules-credit-NelsonTasmanNZ-2__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuNDkiLDI4ODAsMTgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=1920&amp;q=85 1920w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2FUploads%2FTasman-Great-Taste-Trail-at-Kaiteretere-by-Aimee-Jules-credit-NelsonTasmanNZ-2__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuNDkiLDI4ODAsMTgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=2048&amp;q=85 2048w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2FUploads%2FTasman-Great-Taste-Trail-at-Kaiteretere-by-Aimee-Jules-credit-NelsonTasmanNZ-2__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuNDkiLDI4ODAsMTgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=85 3840w" src="/_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbackend.nelsontasman.nz%2Fassets%2FUploads%2FTasman-Great-Taste-Trail-at-Kaiteretere-by-Aimee-Jules-credit-NelsonTasmanNZ-2__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuNDkiLDI4ODAsMTgwMF0.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=85"/></div><div class="absolute inset-0 left-4 z-10 flex flex-col items-center justify-end gap-6 p-12 text-center text-white md:items-start md:p-24 md:text-start xl:p-36 bg-gradient-to-t from-black/30 md:bg-[linear-gradient(45deg,var(--tw-gradient-stops))] lg:to-80% xl:to-60%"><h2 class="font-headline text-3xl font-semibold text-white md:text-5xl lg:w-3/4 xl:w-1/2"><a href="/explore/features/must-dos-in-nelson-tasman/">Must-dos in Nelson Tasman</a></h2><div class="text-xl text-white lg:w-3/4 xl:w-1/2">The must-dos that come with sunshine, stories and good people.
