 of the \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/scenic-attractions/centre-of-new-zealand\",\"children\":\"Centre of New Zealand\"}],\", or snow-dusted hills rising behind \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"3\",{\"href\":\"/scenic-attractions/tahunanui-beach\",\"children\":\"Tāhunanui Beach\"}],\" on a crisp winter morning. Here, getting outdoors doesn’t require leaving the city far behind — walking trails, beaches, rivers and hills are all remarkably close.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"2\",{\"children\":[\"Mountain bikers have some of New Zealand’s best riding on the doorstep, from the classic \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/explore/things-to-do/cycling-and-mountain-biking/great-rides/coppermine-trail-great-ride\",\"children\":\"Coppermine Trail\"}],\" to the purpose-built trails of \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"3\",{\"href\":\"/activities-day-trips/koata-mtb-park\",\"children\":\"Koata Park\"}],\" and \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"5\",{\"href\":\"/activities-day-trips/cable-bay-mtb-park\",\"children\":\"Cable Bay Adventure Park\"}],\". With riding year round and trails for different abilities and appetites for adventure, it’s easy to spend the morning on two wheels and be back in town for a riverside coffee, local beer or long lunch.\"]}]]]}]]}]}]}]}]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"3c:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"2409\",{\"children\":[false,[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"ElementalOperatorListings\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$10\",null,{\"fallback\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"spinner-container flex grow flex-wrap items-center justify-center\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"flex w-full grow items-center justify-center py-5\",\"children\":\"Please wait...\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"loading loading-ball loading-xs\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"loading loading-ball loading-sm\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"loading loading-ball loading-md\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"loading loading-ball loading-lg\"}]]}]}],\"children\":\"$L40\"}]}]}]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"3d:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"4842\",{\"children\":[false,[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"ElementAccordion\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"container pb-12 pt-6 md:pt-12 lg:pb-20\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-wrap text-start justify-between max-w-none prose lg:prose-lg xl:prose-xl mb-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"w-full !text-xl lg:!leading-9 xl:w-1/4 shrink-0\",\"children\":\"Frequently asked questions about Nelson New Zealand\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"w-full max-w-none justify-end text-start empty:hidden xl:w-2/3 [\u0026\u003e*:first-child]:!mt-0\",\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Planning a visit to Nelson City? From getting here and getting around to things to do, rainy-day ideas and the story behind Whakatū, here are a few handy answers to help you make the most of your time in the city.\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L41\",null,{\"type\":\"single\",\"collapsible\":true,\"className\":\"w-full justify-end text-start xl:ms-auto xl:w-2/3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L42\",\"94\",{\"value\":94,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L43\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold xl:text-lg\",\"children\":\"Where is Nelson City and how do I get there?\"}],[\"$\",\"$L44\",null,{\"className\":\"prose xl:prose-lg\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Nelson sits at the top of New Zealand’s South Island, looking out across Tasman Bay. Nelson Airport is around 15 minutes from the city centre, with regular domestic flights connecting to major New Zealand cities like Auckland, Wellington and Christchurch. Driving is another great option, especially if Nelson is part of a wider South Island road trip.\"}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L42\",\"95\",{\"value\":95,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L43\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold xl:text-lg\",\"children\":\"What does Whakatū mean?\"}],[\"$\",\"$L44\",null,{\"className\":\"prose xl:prose-lg\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Whakatū is the Māori name for Nelson. The name is commonly interpreted as meaning ‘to build’, ‘to establish’ or ‘to set up’. Using Whakatū acknowledges the deep Māori history and identity of this place, which stretches back long before the establishment of the European settlement of Nelson.\"}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L42\",\"96\",{\"value\":96,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L43\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold xl:text-lg\",\"children\":\"What is Nelson City known for?\"}],[\"$\",\"$L44\",null,{\"className\":\"prose xl:prose-lg\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Nelson is known for sunshine, creativity, great food and incredible access to the outdoors. With \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/explore/places-to-go/national-parks\",\"children\":\"three national parks\"}],\" surrounding the region and \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"3\",{\"href\":\"/explore/things-to-do/cycling-and-mountain-biking/mountain-biking\",\"children\":\"world-class mountain biking\"}],\" right on the city’s doorstep, adventure is never far away. Add \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"5\",{\"href\":\"/explore/things-to-do/arts-artisans\",\"children\":\"galleries and studios\"}],\", independent shops, excellent local produce, \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"7\",{\"href\":\"/explore/eat-and-drink/wineries\",\"children\":\"wine\"}],\" and \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"9\",{\"href\":\"/explore/eat-and-drink/breweries\",\"children\":\"craft beer\"}],\", and you’ve got a small city with plenty packed into it.\"]}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L42\",\"97\",{\"value\":97,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L43\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold xl:text-lg\",\"children\":\"What are the best things to do in Nelson City?\"}],[\"$\",\"$L44\",null,{\"className\":\"prose xl:prose-lg\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Start in the compact city centre, where you can browse galleries, independent shops and cafés before exploring the riverside and heritage streets. Visit the Nelson Market on a Saturday, discover local art at The Suter, wander through Queens Gardens, or hit one of the walking and cycling trails close to town. Explore our \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/explore/places-to-go/cities-towns/nelson-city/things-to-do-nelson-city\",\"children\":\"Things to do in Nelson City story\"}],\" for more inspiration.\"]}]}]]}],\"$L45\",\"$L46\",\"$L47\",\"$L48\",\"$L49\",\"$L4a\",\"$L4b\",\"$L4c\",\"$L4d\"]}]]}]}]}]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"3e:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"2626\",{\"children\":[false,[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"ElementContent bg-sky text-white\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"container pt-6 md:pt-12 lg:pt-16 pb-6 md:pb-12 lg:pb-20\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-wrap text-start justify-between max-w-none prose lg:prose-lg xl:prose-xl prose-invert text-white\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"w-full !text-xl lg:!leading-9 xl:w-1/4 shrink-0\",\"children\":\"Quick fact in celebration of Te Wiki o te Reo Māori\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"w-full max-w-none justify-end text-start empty:hidden xl:w-2/3 [\u0026\u003e*:first-child]:!mt-0\",\"children\":[null,[[\"$\",\"p\",\"0\",{\"children\":[\"The Maori name for Nelson has two alternative spellings. Wakatū or Whakatū. Neither is wrong, and both spellings have traditions and stories behind them. These stories can be found on \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"1\",{\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"href\":\"https://www.theprow.org.nz/maori/whats-in-a-name-wakatu-or-whakatu/\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"children\":\"The Prow.\"}],\" \"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"2\",{\"children\":\"Pronunciation Guide: (Far-car-two). \"}]]]}]]}]}]}]}]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"3f:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"4078\",{\"children\":[false,[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"ElementalPageGrid\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"py-6 empty:hidden md:pt-12 container\",\"children\":null}],[\"$\",\"$L4e\",null,{\"className\":\"w-full\",\"opts\":{\"loop\":true},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L4f\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L50\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"relative max-h-[1400px] min-h-[500px] w-full 2xl:max-h-[75vh] 2xl:min-h-[800px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L51\",null,{\"matchingFormat\":{\"ID\":4850,\"Url\":\"https://backend.nelsontasman.nz/assets/Uploads/Tasman-Great-Taste-Trail-at-Kaiteretere-by-Aimee-Jules-credit-NelsonTasmanNZ-2__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuNDkiLDI4ODAsMTgwMF0.jpg\",\"WebPUrl\":\"https://backend.nelsontasman.nz/assets/Uploads/Tasman-Great-Taste-Trail-at-Kaiteretere-by-Aimee-Jules-credit-NelsonTasmanNZ-2__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuNDkiLDI4ODAsMTgwMF0_ExtRewriteWyJqcGciLCJ3ZWJwIl0.webp\",\"Width\":2560,\"Height\":1600,\"Format\":\"large\"},\"mediaQuerySources\":[],\"src\":\"https://backend.nelsontasman.nz/assets/Uploads/Tasman-Great-Taste-Trail-at-Kaiteretere-by-Aimee-Jules-credit-NelsonTasmanNZ-2__FocusFillMaxWyItMC4zMSIsIjAuNDkiLDI4ODAsMTgwMF0.jpg\",\"alt\":\"Tasman Great Taste Trail at Kaiteretere by Aimee Jules credit NelsonTasmanNZ (2)\",\"fill\":false,\"width\":\"100%\",\"height\":\"100%\",\"focusPercentageX\":null,\"focusPercentageY\":null,\"imgCover\":\"object-cover\",\"nobg\":false,\"link\":null,\"className\":\"\",\"containerClassName\":\"md:aspect-video\",\"blurData\":\"U~LE:4?ct6?c_N%NocxvtSt7oca~-=xus:t8\",\"unoptimized\":false}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"absolute inset-0 left-4 z-10 flex flex-col items-center justify-end gap-6 p-12 text-center text-white md:items-start md:p-24 md:text-start xl:p-36 bg-gradient-to-t from-black/30 md:bg-[linear-gradient(45deg,var(--tw-gradient-stops))] lg:to-80% xl:to-60%\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"font-headline text-3xl font-semibold text-white md:text-5xl lg:w-3/4 xl:w-1/2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L17\",null,{\"href\":\"/explore/features/must-dos-in-nelson-tasman\",\"target\":null,\"children\":\"Must-dos in Nelson Tasman\"}]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xl text-white lg:w-3/4 xl:w-1/2\",\"children\":\"The must-dos that come with sunshine, stories and good people.\\r\\n\"}],[\"$\",\"$L17\",null,{\"href\":\"/explore/features/must-dos-in-nelson-tasman\",\"className\":\"no-underline font-sans inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap rounded md:text-normal font-medium ring-offset-background transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2 disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 border border-white bg-transparent text-white hover:bg-sky hover:text-white hover:border-sky h-10 px-4 py-2 after:absolute after:inset-0\",\"target\":null,\"children\":[\"Find out more \",[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-arrow-right ms-2 h-6 w-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"1ays0h\",{\"d\":\"M5 12h14\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"xquz4c\",{\"d\":\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"}],\"$undefined\"]}]],\"ref\":null}]]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L52\",null,{\"className\":\"disabled:hidden\"}],[\"$\",\"$L53\",null,{\"className\":\"disabled:hidden\"}]]}]]}]}]}]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"45:[\"$\",\"$L42\",\"98\",{\"value\":98,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L43\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold xl:text-lg\",\"children\":\"Is Nelson worth visiting and how many days should I spend?\"}],[\"$\",\"$L44\",null,{\"className\":\"prose xl:prose-lg\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Absolutely! Nelson Tasman was \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"https://www.nelsontasman.nz/about-us/news-from-nt/nelson-tasman-tops-new-zealands-domestic-visitor-satisfaction-rankings/\",\"children\":\"voted #1 for traveler satisfaction in 2025\"}],\" and it's easy to see why. We recommend spending at least three to four days in Nelson to explore the city at a relaxed pace. Stay longer and use Nelson as your base to discover the wider region, from golden beaches and boutique wineries to creative communities and three spectacular national parks. There's plenty to keep you here.\"]}]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"46:[\"$\",\"$L42\",\"99\",{\"value\":99,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L43\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold xl:text-lg\",\"children\":\"What is the best time of year to visit Nelson?\"}],[\"$\",\"$L44\",null,{\"className\":\"prose xl:prose-lg\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Nelson is a year-round destination, with each season bringing something different. Summer is made for beaches, outdoor dining and long days outside, while autumn brings settled days and beautiful colour. Winter is quieter and well suited to galleries, food and nearby walks, while spring brings longer days and great conditions for getting back out on the hiking trails.\"}]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"47:[\"$\",\"$L42\",\"100\",{\"value\":100,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L43\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold xl:text-lg\",\"children\":\"Can I explore Nelson City without a car?\"}],[\"$\",\"$L44\",null,{\"className\":\"prose xl:prose-lg\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Yes. Central Nelson is compact and easy to explore on foot, with shops, galleries, cafés, parks and the river all close together. Bikes are another good option, and \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/explore/plan-your-trip/getting-around\",\"children\":\"local buses\"}],\" can take you further afield. Heading to Abel Tasman National Park? Many tour operators offer transport from Nelson, and during summer and autumn, the \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"3\",{\"href\":\"/transport/the-better-bus\",\"children\":\"Better Bus\"}],\" connects Nelson with Kaiteriteri, Mārahau and Motueka. A car is handy for exploring further afield, but you can see plenty of Nelson Tasman without one.\"]}]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"48:[\"$\",\"$L42\",\"101\",{\"value\":101,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L43\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold xl:text-lg\",\"children\":\"Where are the best places to eat and drink in Nelson?\"}],[\"$\",\"$L44\",null,{\"className\":\"prose xl:prose-lg\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"You’re spoilt for choice. Nelson has everything from \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/explore/eat-and-drink/cafes\",\"children\":\"relaxed cafés\"}],\" and \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"3\",{\"href\":\"/explore/eat-and-drink/restaurants-and-bars\",\"children\":\"neighbourhood eateries to restaurants\"}],\" celebrating local seafood and seasonal produce. The wider region is also well known for its \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"5\",{\"href\":\"/explore/eat-and-drink/breweries\",\"children\":\"craft breweries\"}],\", \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"7\",{\"href\":\"/explore/eat-and-drink/wineries\",\"children\":\"wineries\"}],\" and \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"9\",{\"href\":\"/explore/eat-and-drink/artisan-markets\",\"children\":\"artisan producers\"}],\", so arriving hungry is a solid strategy.\"]}]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"49:[\"$\",\"$L42\",\"102\",{\"value\":102,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L43\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold xl:text-lg\",\"children\":\"What can I do in Nelson on a rainy day?\"}],[\"$\",\"$L44\",null,{\"className\":\"prose xl:prose-lg\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"Rain is a good excuse to explore Nelson’s creative side. Visit The Suter Art Gallery, browse local galleries and studios, discover the city’s shops, settle into a café or sample some locally made beer. And when the clouds clear, you’re never far from a walk or a waterfront wander.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"2\",{\"children\":[\"Visiting with the kids? Check out our \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/explore/features/rainy-day-fun\",\"children\":\"Rainy day family fun story\"}],\" for more ideas to keep everyone entertained.\"]}]]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"4a:[\"$\",\"$L42\",\"103\",{\"value\":103,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L43\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold xl:text-lg\",\"children\":\"Is there a visitor information centre in Nelson?\"}],[\"$\",\"$L44\",null,{\"className\":\"prose xl:prose-lg\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Nelson City doesn’t have a traditional isite anymore, but you can still find plenty of help when you arrive. \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/accommodation/yha-nelson-by-accents\",\"children\":\"YHA Nelson\"}],\" offers visitor information and local advice.\"]}]}]]}]\n4b:[\"$\",\"$L42\",\"130\",{\"value\":130,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L43\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold xl:text-lg\",\"children\":\"How many people live in Nelson?\"}],[\"$\",\"$L44\",null,{\"className\":\"prose xl:prose-lg\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Nelson is home to approximately 52,584 people, \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"1\",{\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"href\":\"https://www.stats.govt.nz/infographics/detailed-regional-infographics-from-2023-census/our-region-nelson\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"children\":\"according to Stats NZ's 2025 population estimates\"}],\".\"]}]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"4c:[\"$\",\"$L42\",\"131\",{\"value\":131,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L43\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold xl:text-lg\",\"children\":\"Where is the Centre of New Zealand?\"}],[\"$\",\"$L44\",null,{\"className\":\"prose xl:prose-lg\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"The \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/scenic-attractions/centre-of-new-zealand\",\"children\":\"Centre of New Zealand\"}],\" is a popular landmark on Botanical Hill in Nelson, just a short walk from the city centre. A 20–30 minute uphill walk takes you to the summit, where you'll enjoy panoramic views over Nelson, Tasman Bay and the surrounding mountains. It's a favourite local walk that's both family-friendly and dog-friendly, making it a great outing for all ages and four-legged companions. Despite its name, it's not the exact geographical centre of the country. The site was used as a central survey point in the 1800s and remains one of Nelson's most-loved short walks.\"]}]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"4d:[\"$\",\"$L42\",\"132\",{\"value\":132,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L43\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold xl:text-lg\",\"children\":\"What are the best restaurants in Nelson City?\"}],[\"$\",\"$L44\",null,{\"className\":\"prose xl:prose-lg\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Nelson City is home to some of the best dining in the region, with talented chefs making the most of fresh local produce, seafood and wines. Local favourites include \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/eat-drink/hopgoods-restaurant\",\"children\":\"Hopgoods\"}],\" and \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"3\",{\"href\":\"/eat-drink/eight-plates\",\"children\":\"Eight Plates\"}],\" for seasonal fine dining, \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"5\",{\"href\":\"/eat-drink/arden-bar-and-kitchen\",\"children\":\"Arden\"}],\" for creative sharing plates, \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"7\",{\"href\":\"/eat-drink/hawker-house\",\"children\":\"Hawker House\"}],\" for bold Asian flavours and \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"9\",{\"href\":\"/eat-drink/urban-oyster-bar-and-eatery\",\"children\":\"Urban Oyster Bar \u0026 Eatery\"}],\" for seafood and lively dining. For a meal with a view, head to the \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"11\",{\"href\":\"/eat-drink/boat-shed-cafe\",\"children\":\"Boat Shed Café\"}],\" on Nelson's waterfront. From relaxed eateries to award-winning restaurants, there's plenty to satisfy every appetite. And if brunch is more your style, check out our\",[\"$\",\"a\",\"13\",{\"href\":\"/explore/features/brunch-done-right\",\"children\":\" best brunch spots\"}],\" story for more delicious local favourites.\"]}]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"54:I[85825,[\"268\",\"static/chunks/aaea2bcf-79baa8ded2a1c33d.js\",\"341\",\"static/chunks/a4aedd72-4b433100c7dcf21f.js\",\"676\",\"static/chunks/676-6d9ae8027403ff5f.js\",\"378\",\"static/chunks/378-9896b7538a0f41ca.js\",\"919\",\"static/chunks/919-d4193696f45870f9.js\",\"396\",\"static/chunks/app/%5B%5B...cms%5D%5D/page-3f926ba3b63b5d92.js\"],\"default\"]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"40:[\"$\",\"$L54\",null,{\"cms\":{\"ID\":2409,\"ClassName\":\"elementals\\\\ElementalOperatorListings\",\"LastEdited\":\"2026-02-10 14:46:55\",\"Created\":\"2024-07-29 11:10:16\",\"BackgroundColor\":\"white\",\"BackgroundPattern\":null,\"Version\":74,\"Title\":\"In and around Nelson\",\"ShowTitle\":true,\"Sort\":13,\"ExtraClass\":null,\"Style\":null,\"TopPageID\":25,\"ParentID\":49,\"Indentation\":null,\"HTML\":null,\"ContentImageID\":0,\"DisplayMode\":\"card\",\"NoOffset\":false,\"NoSlide\":false,\"StartWith\":null,\"InContainer\":false,\"SelectListingsBy\":\"userfilter\",\"TagCategorySelect\":\"[2341]\",\"LogicalOperator\":\"OR\",\"DealsOnly\":false,\"Limit\":8,\"ContentImageObject\":null,\"ExtraData\":{\"Categories\":[{\"ID\":2337,\"Title\":\"Filter\",\"URLSegment\":\"business-type-filter\",\"AllChildren\":{\"accommodation\":\"Accommodation\",\"activities-day-trips\":\"Activities \u0026 Day Trips\",\"eat-drink\":\"Eat \u0026 Drink\",\"multi-day-tours-packages\":\"Multi-Day Tours \u0026 Packages\",\"retail-services\":\"Retail \u0026 Services\",\"scenic-attractions\":\"Scenic Attractions\",\"transport\":\"Transport\",\"visitor-information-centre\":\"Visitor Information Centre\"},\"Children\":{\"accommodation\":\"Accommodation\",\"activities-day-trips\":\"Activities \u0026 Day Trips\",\"eat-drink\":\"Eat \u0026 Drink\",\"multi-day-tours-packages\":\"Multi-Day Tours \u0026 Packages\",\"retail-services\":\"Retail \u0026 Services\",\"scenic-attractions\":\"Scenic Attractions\",\"transport\":\"Transport\",\"visitor-information-centre\":\"Visitor Information Centre\"}}],\"Tags\":{\"port-nelson\":\"Port Nelson\",\"hira\":\"Hira\",\"nelson-central\":\"Nelson Central\",\"stoke\":\"Stoke\"}},\"Parent\":{\"className\":\"DNADesign\\\\Elemental\\\\Models\\\\ElementalArea\",\"href\":\"https://backend.nelsontasman.nz/api/v1/DNADesign-Elemental-Models-ElementalArea/49.json\",\"id\":49},\"Component\":\"ElementalOperatorListings\",\"addTopPadding\":true,\"addBottomPadding\":true,\"headingLevel\":null},\"ssrHydrated\":true,\"initialResult\":[{\"Title\":\"Cable Bay Adventure Park - Paintball\",\"Summary\":\"Fast, exciting action on the largest paintball site in Nelson, spread out across our new, larger field, challenge your opponents to capture the flag and avoid being shot.\",\"Description\":\"We operate the largest paintball theme park in Nelson. The recognized leader in corporate paintball events, we also provide first class entertainment to the general public. Our new paintball site offers a wider field with capacity to take up to 15 players on each team. We will be adding additional features, including huts, trees and mounds to add to the challenge. All paintball players receive a full briefing before the day's battle commences, covering proper use of the paintball equipment and with an emphasis on safety precautions. The attire that paintball players will be required to wear is also issued at the beginning of the game and includes camouflage overalls and full face masks for extra protection, padded vests also available.\",\"Region\":\"Nelson Tasman\",\"City\":\"Hira\",\"Suburb\":\"Hira\",\"Street\":\"194 Cable Bay Road\",\"PostCode\":null,\"Website\":\"https://www.cablebayadventurepark.com/paintball\",\"Link\":\"/activities-day-trips/cable-bay-adventure-park-paintball\",\"MainImage\":\"https://register.newzealand.com/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/product_images/p-F658199D-D98F-E4F8-C5CCDCC7F9BE793E-2544003.jpg?itok=U8t_NFIv\",\"MainImageBlur\":\"UaGIld-pj??Z~nxujY${%H%LWBac~p?ZR+S#\",\"AdultRateHighPeriodLowPrice\":35,\"AdultRateHighPeriodHighPrice\":50,\"Latitude\":-41.2017616,\"Longitude\":173.4127412,\"Icon\":\"person-walking\",\"PartnerLevel\":40,\"DealBadgeTitle\":null,\"RandomValue\":9807,\"ID\":338,\"ClassName\":\"models\\\\OperatorListing\",\"Tags\":[\"Theme \u0026 leisure parks\",\"Hira\",\"Nelson Tasman\",\"New Zealand\",\"Activities \u0026 Day Trips\",\"Cable Bay\",\"Trade ready\",\"Local Activities\"],\"ListingType\":[\"Theme \u0026 leisure parks\"],\"MainBusinessType\":\"Activities \u0026 Day Trips\",\"HasDeals\":false,\"ResultType\":\"Listing\"},{\"Title\":\"Abel Tasman Water \u0026 Walk\",\"Summary\":\"Abel Tasman National Park is world famous for its beaches, waters, unmodified estuaries, lush bush to the high tide mark and the excellent walking tracks.\",\"Description\":\"Abel Tasman Water \u0026 Walk is for visitors who have a focus on walking through the park so that they can spend more time exploring the many features on offer and discovering there is much more here than anticipated. Access is by water taxi to Medlands Beach, walking through an ever changing forest of silver fern, strangely twisted Manuka or kanuka and beech trees, beneath large podocarp trees alongside Falls River over a swing bridge on to Torrent Bay, Cleopatra's Pool or Pitt Head. This added value, fully guided journey interprets the less obvious features such as the early settler activity as well as Maori history and the endless stories that abound here, especially from the rich variety of vegetation, birds and aquatic life.\",\"Region\":\"Nelson Tasman\",\"City\":\"Nelson Central\",\"Suburb\":\"Tāhunanui\",\"Street\":\"114 Tahunanui Drive\",\"PostCode\":null,\"Website\":\"https://www.wineartandwilderness.co.nz\",\"Link\":\"/activities-day-trips/abel-tasman-water-and-walk\",\"MainImage\":\"https://register.newzealand.com/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/product_images/2021-02/3-2.jpg?itok=VK59GAZ8\",\"MainImageBlur\":\"Uj8=QjtnRijD%%tTV@ackZf-j?f5WaWFofoe\",\"AdultRateHighPeriodLowPrice\":529,\"AdultRateHighPeriodHighPrice\":529,\"Latitude\":-41.28769691,\"Longitude\":173.2463722,\"Icon\":\"person-walking\",\"PartnerLevel\":40,\"DealBadgeTitle\":null,\"RandomValue\":9687,\"ID\":195,\"ClassName\":\"models\\\\OperatorListing\",\"Tags\":[\"Attractions\",\"Heritage attractions\",\"Urban attractions\",\"Nelson Central\",\"Nelson Tasman\",\"New Zealand\",\"Activities \u0026 Day Trips\",\"Abel Tasman National Park\",\"Trade ready\"],\"ListingType\":[\"Heritage attractions\",\"Attractions\",\"Urban attractions\"],\"MainBusinessType\":\"Activities \u0026 Day Trips\",\"HasDeals\":false,\"ResultType\":\"Listing\"},{\"Title\":\"Cycle Nelson: Coppermine Rocks \u0026 Rails\",\"Summary\":\"Discover one of Nelson’s most fascinating rides on this guided tour of the Coppermine Trail, following the route of the historic Dun Mountain Railway.\",\"Description\":\"Along the way, your guide will bring the landscape to life. The trail crosses the Dun Mountain mineral belt, a striking band of ancient rock pushed up from deep beneath the earth’s crust. The rocks here are so unusual that the mineral-rich rock dunite is named after Dun Mountain itself, and their high metal content creates a stark, otherworldly landscape where only the hardiest plants survive.\",\"Region\":\"Nelson Tasman\",\"City\":\"Nelson Central\",\"Suburb\":\"Tāhunanui\",\"Street\":\"70 Beach Road\",\"PostCode\":null,\"Website\":\"https://www.cyclenelson.co.nz/mountain-bike-tours/coppermine-rocks-rails/\",\"Link\":\"/activities-day-trips/coppermine-trail-guided-private-mountain-bike-loop\",\"MainImage\":\"https://register.newzealand.com/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/product_images/2025-02/20250119_105418.jpg?itok=su3scYdN\",\"MainImageBlur\":\"U-D0[htRWBxv%%ozadt8t.bHW9og%iflV?t7\",\"AdultRateHighPeriodLowPrice\":430,\"AdultRateHighPeriodHighPrice\":510,\"Latitude\":-41.28390197,\"Longitude\":173.23979211,\"Icon\":\"person-walking\",\"PartnerLevel\":40,\"DealBadgeTitle\":null,\"RandomValue\":9379,\"ID\":2395,\"ClassName\":\"models\\\\OperatorListing\",\"Tags\":[\"Activities \u0026 Day Trips\",\"Cycling \u0026 Mountain Biking\",\"Sports\",\"Nelson Central\",\"Nelson Tasman\",\"New Zealand\",\"Great Rides\",\"Trade ready\",\"Mountain biking\"],\"ListingType\":[\"Sports\",\"Cycling \u0026 Mountain Biking\",\"Mountain biking\"],\"MainBusinessType\":\"Activities \u0026 Day Trips\",\"HasDeals\":false,\"ResultType\":\"Listing\"},{\"Title\":\"Cycle Nelson: Māpua Artisan Wine Tour - Guided\",\"Summary\":\"You'll enjoy our popular guided e-bike journey along Tasman Bay with sweeping coastal views, Māori and European history, and\\r\\nconservation stories. A cafe stop, lunch and two wine tastings enrich the tour, before your return transfer back to Nelson.\",\"Description\":\"Discover the beauty of Tasman Bay on a guided e‑bike adventure combining stunning coastal views, local history, and Nelson’s signature art and wine culture. Glide along the Great Taste Trail past golden beaches and tidal inlets as your guide shares stories of Māori heritage, European settlement, and inspiring conservation efforts that shape this extraordinary region. Pause at a local café for barista coffee and a fresh‑baked treat before riding inland to a boutique family‑run winery for a personalised tasting among the vines.  Continue across the wild sands of Rabbit Island, then board the small ferry to the vibrant waterside village of Māpua. Here, your experience culminates with a wine‑tasting and a generous seasonal lunch.\",\"Region\":\"Nelson Tasman\",\"City\":\"Nelson Central\",\"Suburb\":\"Tāhunanui\",\"Street\":\"70 Beach Road\",\"PostCode\":null,\"Website\":\"https://www.cyclenelson.co.nz/single-day-cycle-tours/mapua-artisan-tour/\",\"Link\":\"/activities-day-trips/cycle-nelson-mapua-artisan-wine-tour-guided\",\"MainImage\":\"https://register.newzealand.com/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/product_images/2025-10/PXL_20250113_212449232.jpg?itok=LALT7KrO\",\"MainImageBlur\":\"UmE3bb.9tl-:t.tntTtSK9T2beW[.TtnXAo}\",\"AdultRateHighPeriodLowPrice\":425,\"AdultRateHighPeriodHighPrice\":1120,\"Latitude\":-41.28401778,\"Longitude\":173.23967543,\"Icon\":\"person-walking\",\"PartnerLevel\":40,\"DealBadgeTitle\":null,\"RandomValue\":8722,\"ID\":3716,\"ClassName\":\"models\\\\OperatorListing\",\"Tags\":[\"Activities \u0026 Day Trips\",\"Cycling \u0026 Mountain Biking\",\"Sports\",\"Wineries\",\"Nelson Central\",\"Nelson Tasman\",\"New Zealand\",\"Trade ready\"],\"ListingType\":[\"Sports\",\"Cycling \u0026 Mountain Biking\",\"Wineries\"],\"MainBusinessType\":\"Activities \u0026 Day Trips\",\"HasDeals\":false,\"ResultType\":\"Listing\"},{\"Title\":\"Tides Hotel\",\"Summary\":\"Nelson’s central-city hotel, conference centre, restaurant and bar – right beside the river and just a few minutes walk from Nelson’s main shopping precinct.  Welcome to one of Nelson’s most stylish \u0026 contemporary local hotels. We are proudly local.\",\"Description\":\"Tides Hotel Nelson is located beside the Maitai River and is only a short walk to Nelsons shopping and business centre.  The Hotel offers comfortable Studio Units and One Bedroom Suites either on the poolside or the very popular riverfront.  All 47 units are fully air-conditioned with fridge, tea \u0026 coffee making facilities and Sky TV.  The ensuite bathroom has underfloor heating, hair dryer and complimentary toiletries. The Tides Restaurant and Bar  is located beside the Maitai River and is open for breakfast, lunch and dinner. Your comfort and relaxation are our primary consideration. Please let us know your specific accommodation requirements so we can make sure your stay is thoroughly enjoyable.\",\"Region\":\"Nelson Tasman\",\"City\":\"Nelson Central\",\"Suburb\":\"Nelson\",\"Street\":\"66 Trafalgar Street\",\"PostCode\":null,\"Website\":\"https://www.tideshotel.co.nz\",\"Link\":\"/accommodation/tides-hotel\",\"MainImage\":\"https://register.newzealand.com/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/product_images/2023-07/Drinks%20on%20the%20Deck.jpg?itok=mBXEyZ3z\",\"MainImageBlur\":\"UNFh|-~pTI_N_3?bozt75QtlxuRP%#pI%M%M\",\"AdultRateHighPeriodLowPrice\":165,\"AdultRateHighPeriodHighPrice\":395,\"Latitude\":-41.2693335,\"Longitude\":173.283863,\"Icon\":\"bed\",\"PartnerLevel\":40,\"DealBadgeTitle\":null,\"RandomValue\":8314,\"ID\":420,\"ClassName\":\"models\\\\OperatorListing\",\"Tags\":[\"Local Stays\",\"EV Charging\",\"Internet (Public Use)\",\"Spa Pool\",\"Accommodation\",\"Hotels\",\"Nelson Central\",\"Nelson Tasman\",\"New Zealand\",\"Breakfast\",\"Children Welcome\",\"Conference Facilities\",\"Dinner\",\"Disabled Access\",\"Laundry\",\"Licensed Bar\",\"Luggage Storage\",\"Lunch\",\"Restaurant\",\"Room Service\",\"Swimming Pool\",\"Bike friendly accommodation\",\"Trade ready\"],\"ListingType\":[\"Hotels\"],\"MainBusinessType\":\"Accommodation\",\"HasDeals\":false,\"ResultType\":\"Listing\"},{\"Title\":\"Cable Bay Scenic Quad Bike Tours\",\"Summary\":\"A range of stunning, scenic and fully guided self-drive 4X4 quad bike tours. Tour on farm and river trails, through native forest and spectacular coastal views. Good quality trails with full instruction and safety equipment provided. Open year round.\",\"Description\":\"Cable Bay Adventure Park, only 15 minutes from Nelson City, is where you can enjoy one of our immensely popular 4-wheel motorbike adventures. Our tours range from 1.5- 2.5 hours, inclusive of your safety briefing. You can expect river crossings, driving through beautiful native forests and up into the hills for fabulous views over the surrounding bays - Cable Bay \u0026 Delaware Bay. You can also add on our signature ride, The Skywire - one of the world’s longest flying-fox rides, soaring high above the forest at speeds of up to 100km/h. Our tours have up to 5 departures daily through the summer months, with 2-3 departures daily over the winter. After your tour, you are welcome to join us for coffee or lunch at our licensed café.\",\"Region\":\"Nelson Tasman\",\"City\":\"Hira\",\"Suburb\":\"Hira\",\"Street\":\"194 Cable Bay Road\",\"PostCode\":null,\"Website\":\"https://www.cablebayadventurepark.com/quad-bike-tours\",\"Link\":\"/activities-day-trips/scenic-quad-bike-tours\",\"MainImage\":\"https://register.newzealand.com/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/product_images/p-B1127C0C-977E-344F-2C8F81E4193E0B82-2544003.jpg?itok=fo_0YFza\",\"MainImageBlur\":\"UeEfNB?cNfxt.S.8%MtQt.%h%Mt7~q%hXAt7\",\"AdultRateHighPeriodLowPrice\":140,\"AdultRateHighPeriodHighPrice\":195,\"Latitude\":-41.2022506,\"Longitude\":173.4121037,\"Icon\":\"person-walking\",\"PartnerLevel\":40,\"DealBadgeTitle\":null,\"RandomValue\":8101,\"ID\":259,\"ClassName\":\"models\\\\OperatorListing\",\"Tags\":[\"Off-road driving\",\"Sports\",\"Hira\",\"Nelson Tasman\",\"New Zealand\",\"Activities \u0026 Day Trips\",\"Cable Bay\",\"Local Activities\",\"Trade ready\"],\"ListingType\":[\"Sports\",\"Off-road driving\"],\"MainBusinessType\":\"Activities \u0026 Day Trips\",\"HasDeals\":false,\"ResultType\":\"Listing\"},{\"Title\":\"Delorenzos Studio Apartments \",\"Summary\":\"DeLorenzo's offers 30 luxury studio apartments, including 7 interconnecting apartments and 4 accessible rooms - each designed to envelop the discerning traveller in warmth, comfort and style.\",\"Description\":\"Delorenzo’s offer a heated swimming pool which is open during the summer months, complimentary access to MiGym on Bridge Street. All rooms are fully air-conditioned have a kitchenette including elements, microwave, dish drawer, coffee pod machine and washing machine and dryer. There is a guest computer to use in the main foyer, complimentary WIFI in each room, 50+SKY TV channels and an electric vehicle charging station. Chargeback facilities and room service are available from The Tides Bar \u0026 Eatery located at Tides Hotel, situated on the beautiful Maitai River in the heart of the city.\\r\\n\",\"Region\":\"Nelson Tasman\",\"City\":\"Nelson Central\",\"Suburb\":\"The Wood\",\"Street\":\"43-55 Trafalgar St Nelson 7010 New Zealand\",\"PostCode\":null,\"Website\":\"https://delorenzos.co.nz/\",\"Link\":\"/accommodation/delorenzos-studio-apartments\",\"MainImage\":\"https://register.newzealand.com/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/product_images/p-5C20CC03-E0C1-DCD0-2BAAC8856F74BC56-2544003.jpg?itok=N6iY4HPN\",\"MainImageBlur\":\"U~Dm%b%Nj?tTyGo$j?o$JGR:ayW@yGo$j?o$\",\"AdultRateHighPeriodLowPrice\":250,\"AdultRateHighPeriodHighPrice\":595,\"Latitude\":-41.2683401,\"Longitude\":173.2842418,\"Icon\":\"bed\",\"PartnerLevel\":40,\"DealBadgeTitle\":null,\"RandomValue\":8045,\"ID\":295,\"ClassName\":\"models\\\\OperatorListing\",\"Tags\":[\"Trade ready\",\"Accommodation\",\"Apartments\",\"Nelson Central\",\"Nelson Tasman\",\"New Zealand\",\"BBQ Facility\",\"Breakfast\",\"Children Welcome\",\"Conference Facilities\",\"Dinner\",\"Disabled Access\",\"Gymnasium\",\"Internet (Public Use)\",\"Laundry\",\"Luggage Storage\",\"Restaurant\",\"Room Service\",\"Safety Deposit Box at Reception\",\"Swimming Pool\"],\"ListingType\":[\"Apartments\"],\"MainBusinessType\":\"Accommodation\",\"HasDeals\":false,\"ResultType\":\"Listing\"},{\"Title\":\"The Better Bus\",\"Summary\":\"The Better Bus runs between Nelson and the Abel Tasman National Park’s southern access points of Kaiteriteri and Marahau, stopping at Richmond and Motueka. Summer months only.\",\"Description\":\"Visit betterbus.co.nz to reserve your seat on the bus. Book ahead to lock in your trip. Bookings for tomorrow must be placed before 5.30 pm.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor bookings after 5.30 pm on the following day, call us, and we will do our best to accommodate.\",\"Region\":null,\"City\":null,\"Suburb\":\"Tāhunanui\",\"Street\":\"70 Beach Road\",\"PostCode\":\"7011 \",\"Website\":\"https://www.betterbus.co.nz/\",\"Link\":\"/transport/the-better-bus\",\"MainImage\":\"https://backend.nelsontasman.nz/assets/listings/the-better-bus/Better-Bus-buses__FocusFillMaxWyIwLjAwIiwiMC4wMCIsMjg4MCwxODAwXQ.png\",\"MainImageBlur\":\"UPD9#A-.WA?a~pxuax%LRpogf8Rk~pxuax%L\",\"AdultRateHighPeriodLowPrice\":0,\"AdultRateHighPeriodHighPrice\":0,\"Latitude\":-41.284331,\"Longitude\":173.240048,\"Icon\":\"taxi-bus\",\"PartnerLevel\":40,\"DealBadgeTitle\":null,\"RandomValue\":7662,\"ID\":1341,\"ClassName\":\"models\\\\OperatorListing\",\"Tags\":[\"Trade ready\",\"Bus \u0026 coach transport\",\"Abel Tasman National Park\",\"Nelson Central\",\"Motueka\",\"Tāhunanui\",\"Richmond\",\"Mārahau\",\"Kaiteriteri\",\"Nelson Tasman\",\"Abel Tasman\",\"Transport\"],\"ListingType\":[\"Bus \u0026 coach transport\"],\"MainBusinessType\":\"Transport\",\"HasDeals\":false,\"ResultType\":\"Listing\"}],\"initialTotal\":358,\"initialTagDistribution\":{\"Accommodation\":87,\"Activities \u0026 Day Trips\":135,\"Eat \u0026 Drink\":54,\"Multi-Day Tours \u0026 Packages\":17,\"Retail \u0026 Services\":23,\"Scenic Attractions\":14,\"Transport\":38}}]\n"])</script></body></html>